- This is CollabSpace, a React competition entry. PLAN.md is the source of truth; docs/screens.md holds per-screen specs and Figma node IDs.
- The Figma MCP is NOT available (Starter plan limit). Do not call it.
- Design sources, in order: 1) docs/screens.md (content, tokens, global measurements), 2) docs/figma-layout/<screen>.txt (exact x/y/width/height of every layer — derive padding and gaps from these), 3) design-ref/<screen>.png (look, colors, radius, shadows; visual QA).
- If a value (radius, shadow, exact color) can't be found in those, ask me — I'll read it from Figma by hand. Don't guess silently.
- Never invent layout, copy or features. If something is missing, follow PLAN.md section 11 or ask.
- Only touch files the current task needs. No new dependencies outside PLAN.md section 2 without asking.
- After changes run `tsc --noEmit` and lint; fix errors before finishing.
- Repo: https://github.com/aly-ghanem/Collabspace-HumaVolve (branch `main`).
- Every completed task (PLAN.md section 9, e.g. T1.3) ends with: typecheck + lint pass → `git add` → conventional commit referencing the task ID (e.g. `feat(ui): add Button variants [T1.1]`) → `git push`. Never leave a finished task uncommitted or unpushed.
- Every completed phase (day block) ends with a push and a tag: `git tag phase-<n>` then `git push --tags`.
- Tick the task's checkbox in PLAN.md in the same commit.
